---
description: "Triage one candidate finding - re-verify its evidence against the code and issue a verdict"
mode: subagent
model: "anthropic/claude-opus-5"
tools: read, grep, bash, edit
tool_loop:
  max_rounds: 60
params:
  finding: string
system: "You are a strict triage judge of code-quality findings. Reviewers make mistakes, so you trust nothing a candidate report claims and re-verify every claim against the current code yourself. You never fix code and never edit the substance of a candidate - your only write is appending your verdict note under its Triage heading."
---
let candidate = read({ path: finding })?
let template = read({ path: "quality/TEMPLATE.md" })?
let prior = bash({ command: "ls -1 quality/issues 2>/dev/null || true; ls -1 quality/resolved 2>/dev/null || true" })?
let log_tail = bash({ command: "tail -c 4000 quality/TRIAGE_LOG.md 2>/dev/null || true" })?

import { TriageVerdict } from "./quality.thetalib"

let v: TriageVerdict = @`TRIAGE — verify this candidate quality finding. Trust nothing in it.

Candidate file: ${finding}
Candidate content:
${candidate}

Method — run every step:
1. Form. All template fields present and plausible (template below); exactly one
   root cause; evidence excerpts present; no severity/priority adjectives; no fix
   design beyond one direction paragraph. Violations that block evaluation =
   malformed.
2. Reality. Open every cited file. Verify each excerpt exists at or near the
   cited lines (content match required; small line drift is tolerated). Re-run
   any stated searches. For deadness claims, re-run the reference hunt YOURSELF:
   grep the identifier across src/, extensions/, tools/, tests/; check
   string-keyed and dynamic access and re-exports. A claim that does not
   reproduce = false-positive, and your reason must state the refuting evidence.
3. Anchor. The "why" names a real, mechanically-evidenced problem (dead code
   proven, vestige demonstrated at every call site, scaffolding whose feature
   landed). Taste-only reasoning = questionable.
4. Scope — apply the block matching the candidate's lens: frontmatter.
   lens: D2 — covers simplicity and cruft in production sources under src/.
   Code whose only callers are tests is NOT dead in this repository (witness
   tests are deliberate callers) — such a filing is false-positive. Bug
   reports, coverage gaps, naming complaints, design opinions = out-of-scope.
   lens: D7 — covers test-code smells in test sources under tests/ ONLY, and
   the "why" must be one of the five D7 classes: silent skip, assertion that
   cannot fail, boilerplate duplication, copy-paste fixture/double, misleading
   name. A location outside tests/ = out-of-scope. Coverage claims ("a test
   should exist"), suite-composition/E2E-vs-unit opinions, and flaky or
   wrong-behaviour claims (those are bugs) = out-of-scope. False-positive
   carve-outs — a candidate ignoring one of these is false-positive: census/
   pin gate tests (*gate*.test.ts, closing-gate, cross-cutting-gates,
   rfc-*-spec-surface-gate, committed-fixture-parse-gate,
   registry-closed-set-corpus-gate) assert pinned counts BY DESIGN; negative
   witnesses through recording doubles are legitimate; a red test citing an
   open docs/bugs/ signature is a documented correct-reason red, not a skip;
   a proposal to merge/rename/delete a test cited by
   docs/reference/coverage-matrix.md or a bug doc's witness list that does not
   say so; tests/live/** failLoudly posture is correct skipping.
   Human-ruled D7 precedents (rule this way; do not go questionable on them):
   a misleading-name filing stands when the title states a superseded claim,
   even if the title appends a "— bug NNNN: … instead" correction or an
   in-body comment documents the supersession — the class is about what the
   title asserts; and the same stale wording recurring across same-commit
   sibling tests is repeated drift, not a design choice (PTQ-0266, PTQ-0280).
   lens: D9 — covers placement & breakdown in src/ ONLY; the candidate's
   d9_class selects the check. Verify the ACCOUNTING, never the proposed seam or
   home. breakdown: (a) re-run node tools/quality/size-scan.mjs map --files <a
   one-line manifest of the host's file> and confirm LOC + band (bands from
   size-scan bands; an exempt-band host = false-positive); (b) open the cited
   ranges and confirm the inventory's rows are real distinct concerns (state
   clusters / member groups that do not share locals or fields) — a row that is
   one concern split by adjectives is a refuted inventory; (c) confirm the
   reasons-considered list did not overlook an applicable concrete/strong reason
   (closed-enumeration dispatch mirroring a spec table, single algorithm with
   ≥ 6 shared locals, ≥ 80 % data/type LOC, one grammar production, generated
   code; strong: spec-cited invariant, measured cost, reverted prior split,
   existing exemption in quality/exemptions.json below the 25 % growth bar).
   misplacement: re-count the affinity both ways at the cited declaration (own-
   host members touched vs foreign-host members leaned on) or re-verify the
   sibling pattern; a claim resting on taste alone is false-positive. husk:
   re-count payload vs scaffolding LOC, confirm the remaining members have live
   callers (none → out-of-scope, D2's deadness), and confirm the module is not a
   deliberate re-export barrel / compatibility facade (header comment, importer
   count). Verdicts: accurate accounting → questionable — accounting verified;
   target shape needs a human ruling (NEVER confirmed: a D9 fix is a move or a
   breakdown whose shape is a design decision; the human's accept --note is the
   ratification). Refuted accounting, zone-band breakdown without a ≥ 2-concern
   inventory, an overlooked reason, a barrel/facade → false-positive with the
   refuting evidence. Dead code → out-of-scope (D2); bugs, naming, duplication →
   out-of-scope.
   lens: D4 — duplication & drift in src/ ONLY; d4_class selects the check.
   clone/drift: open every cited copy and confirm the excerpts match at the
   cited lines; re-run node tools/quality/clone-scan.mjs map --files <a
   one-line manifest of the first copy's file> and confirm the group (or,
   for a claimed clone the scanner does not list, diff the copies yourself);
   confirm every copy is live (a dead copy is D2's → out-of-scope); a copy
   that is a spec-normative vector table cited to its clause on both sides is
   false-positive; incidental similarity with no stated breakage is
   false-positive. clone, accurate → confirmed (the fix is a mechanical
   dedupe). drift: additionally verify the filing's claim of WHICH copy is
   right (the cited clause / pinning test / commit) — verified → confirmed;
   absent or unverifiable → questionable — drift verified; which copy is
   right needs a human ruling (the fixer never picks a behaviour).
   parallel: verify the counted coverage claim (X has M cases, Y covers N)
   against the current code; accurate → questionable — accounting verified;
   the shared source of truth is a design decision for a human ruling (never
   confirmed); inaccurate → false-positive with the corrected counts.
   lens: D8 — simplification in src/ ONLY. Verify the ACCOUNTING, never the
   simpler shape: re-count the named concepts/layers/states/special cases at
   the cited ranges and the live call sites (size-scan map importer counts); for
   reimplemented, open the named facility and confirm it covers every cited
   need (a missed load-bearing need the filing did not account = false-positive);
   for against-grain, confirm the documented intent quoted is real; for
   heavier-than-scale, confirm the data size claim at the call sites. Then the
   spec check: if the simpler shape (when named) would drop behaviour a
   docs/spec_topics clause requires and the filing does not set challenges_spec
   naming it → false-positive; with challenges_spec → still questionable, note
   "challenges spec <anchor>". D2 precedents apply (spec-mirroring arms,
   rationale-stated knobs → false-positive). Exempted host (quality/
   exemptions.json, exemptions --lens D8 — each row carries the exempted
   class) without a distinct d8_class or ≥ 25 % growth → false-positive.
   Accurate → questionable — accounting verified; the simpler shape is a
   design decision for a human ruling (NEVER confirmed). Dead code → D2;
   size → D9; duplication → D4 (out-of-scope).
   Any other lens: value = out-of-scope (no triage rules exist for it).
5. Dedupe. If the same root cause is already tracked, verdict duplicate and name
   the existing file/row. Existing issues and resolved issues:
${prior}
   Recent rejections:
${log_tail}

Template for reference:
${template}

Then append — using the edit tool, changing nothing else — one line under the
candidate file's "## Triage" heading, exactly:
verdict: <your verdict> — <one-line reason> (triage: claude-opus-5)

Finally reply with the requested schema:
- verdict: one of confirmed | questionable | false-positive | duplicate |
  out-of-scope | malformed
- reason: the same one-line reason.

Verdict semantics: confirmed = real, in-scope, anchored, independently verified.
questionable = a real observation whose anchor is taste or whose fix cost
plausibly exceeds its benefit — a human should rule. Everything else rejects the
candidate with your reason on record.`?
v
